        <h2 id="about-heading">About Me</h2> 
        <article class="about-columns">
            <img class="about-float-img" src="/images/anime_cityscape.jpg" alt="Tokyo cityscape"/>
            <p>I've been watching anime since I was 15 years old, starting with the classics before diving deep into
                everything the medium has to offer. What began as casual weekend viewing eventually turned into a
                full blown obsession with storytelling, animation craft, and the unique way anime handles emotion and
                character.</p>

            <p>This site is my attempt to make sense of it all. Every ranking here is personal built from hundreds of
                hours of watching, rewatching, and thinking too hard about fictional characters. I don't just rank by
                popularity or MAL score. I rank by impact: how much a show changed the way I think, feel, or see the
                world.</p>

            <p>My taste leans toward dark, complex narratives Attack on Titan, Death Note, Steins;Gate. But I have a
                soft spot for anything that surprises me, whether that's a comedy that suddenly hits hard emotionally,
                or a slow-burn thriller that pays off every single setup. If a show makes me lose sleep, it earns its
                place on this list.</p>

            <p>Rankings are updated seasonally. If your favourite didn't make the cut, I probably watched it and had
                opinions. Feel free to fight me about it.</p>
        </article>
    </section>

